Now I'll create the pre-commit hook at .git/hooks/pre-commit:
======================================================================

======================================================================
                              TOOL CALL                               
======================================================================
Function: execute_command
Arguments: {"command": "cat > .git/hooks/pre-commit << 'EOF'\n#!/bin/sh\n# Run mypy type checking on all Python files in src/\n\n# Find all Python files in src/\nPYTHON_FILES=$(find src/ -name \"*.py\" -type f)\n\n# Exit if no Python files found\nif [ -z \"$PYTHON_FILES\" ]; then\n    echo \"No Python files found in src/\"\n    exit 0\nfi\n\n# Run mypy on the Python files\necho \"Running mypy type checking on src/...\"\nmypy --config-file=pyproject.toml $PYTHON_FILES\n\n# Store exit code\nEXIT_CODE=$?\n\n# Exit with the same code as mypy\nif [ $EXIT_CODE -ne 0 ]; then\n    echo \"\u274c Type checking failed. Commit blocked.\"\n    exit $EXIT_CODE\nfi\n\necho \"\u2713 Type checking passed.\"\nexit 0\nEOF"}
